<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>The Mountaineers Down the Rams in Four Sets in its First Match of the West Virginia Invitational</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/10/volleyball-the-mountaineers-down-the-rams-in-four-sets-in-its-first-match-of-the-west-virginia-invitational</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/10/volleyball-the-mountaineers-down-the-rams-in-four-sets-in-its-first-match-of-the-west-virginia-invitational</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Trinity Sheridan celebrates after knocking off VCU in the West Virginia Invitational" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/10/DSC08915.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (4-1, 0-0 Big 12) rallied in the fourth set to earn a 3-1 victory over VCU (1-4, 0-0 Atlantic 10) on Thursday evening at Hope Coliseum. The Mountaineers took the match by set scores of 25-12, 25-27, 25-18 and 25-23.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/10/DSC08915.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/10/DSC08915.jpg"><media:title>Trinity Sheridan celebrates after knocking off VCU in the West Virginia Invitational</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/10/DSC08915.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 20